            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0681" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/511: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-07T11:00:00+02:00">April 7, 1934—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 7—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Department’s 20, April 6, 1 p.m.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d497-f1"/> Export Line
                    accepts reservations on steamer sailing from Izmir declaring steamer will call
                    at that port thence after calling at Marmaris proceeding directly to New York
                    arriving about May 10.</p>
                <p>Send further telegrams to Istanbul as I am returning tonight. Arrangements here
                    completed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
